# Event Detection Rules (WatchAgent)

- Keep event-detection functions pure: same inputs (`city`, `current_reading`, `previous_reading`) must produce the same outputs.
- Event detection logic must not access the database, network, filesystem, or environment variables.
- Default to transition-based alerts. A single absolute threshold is not enough unless the threshold itself represents a posture change (for example crossing freezing).
- Do not emit bootstrap alerts from the very first reading for a city; the default is to wait for a meaningful transition.
- Every emitted event payload must include:
  - `city`
  - `timestamp`
  - `event_type`
  - `severity`
  - `message`
  - `reason`
  - `metric`
  - `current_value` (when applicable)
  - `previous_value` (when applicable)
  - `threshold` (when applicable)
- Prefer regime shifts, crossings, and escalations over repeated hourly reminders of the same condition.
- `reason` text must explain why the event is notable in operator terms, not only restate the metric name.
- If an alert would likely fire every hour under stable bad weather, add a transition condition or suppress it.
